@@ -9,6 +9,35 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## WebMCP tools
+
+The shared layout registers browser-native tools through `document.modelContext`
+when available in a secure context (HTTPS or localhost). Use a Chromium build
+with WebMCP enabled, including the `chrome://flags/#enable-webmcp-testing` flag
+where required. Browsers without the API keep the normal application UI.
+
+| Tool | Inputs | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `query: string` | Searches titles and summaries; returns article metadata, slugs, and URLs. |
+| `get_reading_list` | None | Returns saved article metadata and URLs for the current session. |
+| `set_article_bookmark` | `slug: string`, `saved: boolean` | Sets the requested bookmark state and updates mounted reading-list UI. |
+| `open_article` | `slug: string` | Opens a known article in the current tab using Astro navigation. |
+
+Tools reuse the same client service as search and bookmarks. Bookmark writes
+are idempotent; the existing reading-list endpoint still accepts legacy toggle
+requests that omit `saved`. Registrations use AbortSignals for cleanup and are
+renewed after Astro page transitions. Network operations honor execution
+cancellation, and recoverable failures return structured error values.
+
+Agents discover these tools through the browser; no MCP server or transport is
+needed. In-page consumers can use `await document.modelContext.getTools()` and
+`await document.modelContext.executeTool(tool, inputs)` as described in the
+[Chrome WebMCP documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
+
+Run `pnpm test` with Node 22.6+ for automated tool registration, execution,
+validation, cancellation, and reading-list synchronization tests, and `pnpm build`
+for the production build.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
